{"id":"6043e81d580c197fe0f7242974746899072067ee","axis":"silent","repo":"grafana/mimir","sha":"6043e81d580c197fe0f7242974746899072067ee","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","lines":["@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@"," * [FEATURE] Ingester, distributor: Add experimental per-tenant threshold `-ingester.label-value-bytes-metric-threshold` on the total size of a label name's distinct values held in memory. Ingesters report label names over the threshold through the `cortex_ingester_label_value_bytes_over_threshold` metric, and don't reject anything themselves. The distributor rejects series with a value for a label name listed in `-validation.blocked-label-names-for-label-value-bytes`. The overrides-exporter reports blocked label names through the `cortex_limits_blocked_label_names_for_label_value_bytes` metric. Disabled by default. #16714 #16874"," * [FEATURE] MQE: Add experimental functionality to expose per-selector query cost information. #16613 #16619 #16652 #16653"," * [FEATURE] Ingester, distributor: Add experimental per-tenant threshold `-ingester.label-value-bytes-metric-threshold` on the total size of a label name's distinct values held in memory. Ingesters report label names over the threshold through the `cortex_ingester_label_value_bytes_over_threshold` metric, and don't reject anything themselves. The distributor rejects series with a value for a label name listed in `-validation.blocked-label-names-for-label-value-bytes`. Disabled by default. #16714","-* [FEATURE] MQE: Add experimental functionality to expose per-selector query cost information. #16613 #16619 #16652 #16653 #16692","+* [FEATURE] MQE: Add experimental functionality to expose per-selector query cost information. Cost information is only exposed when MQE remote execution is enabled, MQE is used for query sharding, MQE is used for splitting and caching, for JSON responses from the query-frontend. #16613 #16619 #16652 #16653 #16692 #17023"," * [FEATURE] Alertmanager: Add Jira as a supported integration. #16870"," * [FEATURE] Ingester: Add the experimental `-ingester.partition-ring.create-partitions-with-derived-tokens` and `-ingester.partition-ring.max-derived-token-partitions` flags, allowing ingesters to create partitions with tokens derived from the partition ID instead of storing them in the partition ring, which reduces the size of the memberlist state. Before you enable `-ingester.partition-ring.create-partitions-with-derived-tokens` on the ingesters, ensure that `-ingester.partition-ring.max-derived-token-partitions` is applied to all partition ring readers and ingesters, with a value higher than the highest partition ID. Partition IDs at or above the maximum are rejected, and readers that don't have the maximum yet fail when an ingester creates a partition with derived tokens. #16763"," * [FEATURE] Mimirtool: Add the experimental `--partition.derived-tokens` flag to `mimirtool partition-ring add-partition` to add partitions with tokens derived from the partition ID instead of stored in the ring. #16763"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/frontend/querymiddleware/codec.go","lines":["@@ -1109,7 +1109,7 @@ func (c Codec) EncodeMetricsQueryResponse(ctx context.Context, req *http.Request"," \t\tsp.SetAttributes(attribute.Int(\"series\", len(a.Data.Result)))"," \t}"," ","-\tselectedContentType, formatter := c.negotiateContentType(req.Header.Get(\"Accept\"))","+\tselectedContentType, formatter := c.NegotiateContentType(req.Header.Get(\"Accept\"))"," \tif formatter == nil {"," \t\treturn nil, apierror.New(apierror.TypeNotAcceptable, \"none of the content types in the Accept header are supported\")"," \t}","@@ -1200,7 +1200,7 @@ func (c Codec) EncodeLabelsSeriesQueryResponse(ctx context.Context, req *http.Re"," \t\t}"," \t}()"," ","-\tselectedContentType, formatter := c.negotiateContentType(req.Header.Get(\"Accept\"))","+\tselectedContentType, formatter := c.NegotiateContentType(req.Header.Get(\"Accept\"))"," \tif formatter == nil {"," \t